; Lance — the committed suicider (GAMEPLAY-DESIGN Iteration 14 / A5, A.q5).
;
; The design in one line: "it tells you it is coming, and then it cannot change
; its mind." Every number below serves that sentence.
;
; THE PAIR THAT IS THE WHOLE TYPE, read together:
;
;   speed 34 = the fastest thing in the roster, above the falx's 25.
;   accel 9  = the LOWEST in the roster, below the falx's 11.
;
; `accel` is what `velocity.move_toward` spends to CHANGE direction, so a body
; this fast with an accel this low physically cannot follow a moving target. The
; commitment is emergent rather than scripted, exactly as the falx's wide arc is,
; which is what makes P4.2's counterplay honest: "aimed at where you are, so
; being somewhere else is the answer."
;
; hull 22 is the lightest flyer in the game, under the falx's 26. P4.2 asks for
; "light, but fast enough that chip guns get one honest window" - and the window
; is the ALIGN phase, where it holds still and glows. Miss that window and the
; run itself is genuinely hard to track with a chip gun.
;
; damage/fire_rate/muzzle_speed are ZERO and that is not an oversight: the Lance
; carries no gun. Its whole output is the contact blast, so `Lethality.incoming`
; correctly reports delivery mode `contact` for it rather than a cadence.
;
; bomb_damage 55 / bomb_radius 7 are the BLAST, reusing the Payload group the
; aegis introduced. That reuse is deliberate: a suicider is ordnance that flies
; itself, and `Bomb.blast()` is one definition shared by both, so the two can
; never drift into different physics for the same word. 55 against a Kestrel's
; 100 hull is over half the aircraft in one hit - it must be frightening or the
; telegraph is not worth reacting to - while a 7 m radius is small enough that
; moving 8 m sideways is a complete answer.
;
; preferred_range 30 is re-read for this type again: not an orbit radius and not
; a break-off distance, but the SETUP band it backs off to before committing, so
; the run always has room to reach full speed. A suicider that commits from 5 m
; has no telegraph at all.
;
; sight_range 95 sits between the raider's and the falx's 110. It should notice
; you from a good way out - the type is an area-denial threat and a Lance you
; never knew was there is a Lance that taught you nothing.
;
; strength_cost 1.5 is deliberately CHEAP, per P4.2: "cheap and expendable - the
; type a losing enemy fields MORE of." A raider is 1.0, so a Lance is one and a
; half raiders' worth of garrison, which lets a pressured node field a swarm of
; them without blowing its strength budget.
;
; NOTHING HERE IS BALANCED. Per H6 these are authored starting points and the
; harness measures the result; none of it should be tuned before it is measured,
; and the human's hands decide the feel of the telegraph either way.

